Wait — in openCameraPipeline I changed the sensor-parameter assignment from local vals to inline calls. The original:
```
val newSensorOrientation = sensorCapture.getSensorOrientation(effectiveId)
...
livePreview.setSensorOrientation(newSensorOrientation)
```
The getter is called only once either way — same. Inlining is fine (each getter is called exactly once, in the same order? Original: getSensorOrientation, getCfaPattern, getBlackLevelPattern, getWhiteLevel, getLensDistortion are called in that order, then the setters are called. My inline version: setSensorOrientation(getSensorOrientation(...)) — the getter is called at setter time. So the getter order = setter order, which is the same sequence as the original (all getters, then all setters). Hmm — the order of side effects changes: the original does all 5 getters before any setter; my version interleaves them. If the getters are pure (queries to CameraCharacteristics — they are) and the setters don't affect the getters, then it's identical. These are sensor-metadata getters — pure. Safe. But to be maximally conservative, I could keep the local vals. Keeping the vals is also more readable (explicit data flow). To minimize behavioral risk, let me keep the local vals as in the original:

```
val isFront = currentCameraInfo?.facing == CameraCharacteristics.LENS_FACING_FRONT
val newSensorOrientation = sensorCapture.getSensorOrientation(effectiveId)
val newCfaPattern = sensorCapture.getCfaPattern(effectiveId)
val newBlackLevel = sensorCapture.getBlackLevelPattern(effectiveId)
val newWhiteLevel = sensorCapture.getWhiteLevel(effectiveId, selectedCameraId)
val newDistortion = sensorCapture.getLensDistortion(effectiveId)

livePreview.setIsMirrored(isFront)
livePreview.setSensorOrientation(newSensorOrientation)
livePreview.setCfaPattern(newCfaPattern)
livePreview.setBlackLevelPattern(newBlackLevel)
livePreview.setWhiteLevel(newWhiteLevel.toFloat())
livePreview.setDistortion(newDistortion)
livePreview.setBlackLevelOffset(0.0f)
livePreview.setAutoLevelsMode(autoLevelsMode)
livePreview.setShowHistogram(showHistogram)
livePreview.setLogRange(logRange)
applyPipelineSettings()
```

Also, regarding `val window = context.findActivity()?.window ?: return` — I'm extracting the nullable window into a val. Original: `perfOptimizer.enableSustainedPerformanceMode(context.findActivity()?.window ?: return@LaunchedEffect)`. My version: `val window = context.findActivity()?.window ?: return; perfOptimizer.enableSustainedPerformanceMode(window)`. Same behavior. A nice cleanup.

One more thing to double-check in openCameraPipeline: the original's `sensorCapture.openCamera(selectedCameraId, selectedPhysicalId, rawPreviewSurface)` — rawPreviewSurface is `Surface?`; openCamera presumably accepts Surface?. I'll keep it as is.

